    {
      "topic": "Reference NP and implementation branch semantics",
      "status": "kept_with_model_distinction",
      "analysis": "ComplexityLib polynomial-time NTM chooses one of two transitions per step. The deterministic checker consumes the supplied list exactly, checking acceptance when it ends; the time bound is imposed on list length, with frozen-halt padding. FinTM2 implements the checker with cost evidence. Reverse: compile to a reference deterministic pair decider, reject malformed encodings, compute p(|x|), nondeterministically guess within the bound, and run the decider. ImplementedBy unfolds from empty history and covers both answers at every queried branch, not continuations beyond prior halt.",
